#edb/ref 17592186359954} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a5753f9-03a9-5a9b-acaa-fc7135f1ff3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be0479d2-daa4-53ca-93d6-5cafceecb447" :question/math-academy-id "q-96820" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $h:x↦{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $h:x↦{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to ${x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh(x)={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "962bd8fb-e1fe-5079-9863-836d376cb047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469848} {:answer/id #uuid "abea238c-8f75-57f1-84e9-f2ddc1e820ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abea238c-8f75-57f1-84e9-f2ddc1e820ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469849} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a451e5f-bfe8-5c13-99cb-8caeb46be65a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470536} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b2ec325-874c-5a72-a581-45f824d66019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469850} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1cd304-c064-567d-b359-c747a157f612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a1cd304-c064-567d-b359-c747a157f612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469851} :answer-field/id #uuid "04217f27-6d3c-55bb-8506-5b2d0b72ce4a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21f88362-c7c7-5137-8145-50557efa8aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469852} {:answer/id #uuid "3a283992-eda9-545d-aac3-7745f2550a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21f88362-c7c7-5137-8145-50557efa8aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469852} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd45a19-254c-54cd-b60d-66f146d091aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af009dba-f7f5-5f73-94d4-82504fdd6317" :question/math-academy-id "q-96826" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:R\\to R?$\n- **I.** The domain of $g$ is $R$\n- **II.** The codomain of $g$ is $R$\n- **III.** The range of $g$ is $R$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation \n\n$$\ng:R\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $R$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $R,$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66dc03df-3df9-5aee-880e-9b8893a454e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559271} {:answer/id #uuid "95810dec-fe98-5d62-b391-46de5d6c4ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559389} {:answer/id #uuid "dde14787-3b26-5768-9e9c-91acf6135f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559561} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559618} {:answer/id #uuid "fca7a609-f33e-5be9-ae87-737b69fc91e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559618} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e843ef-72f4-5f6d-8133-a40e9b75a28b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1110805d-d0df-5ae9-af4b-5eeeabf99273" :question/math-academy-id "q-96828" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b124a0e4439f1b35affa5a38f175a151cbbad88affb12738585da8280bacb23.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X=\\{0,1\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14bda835-3f7e-5acf-b18b-2e089087e07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469860} {:answer/id #uuid "42cb668d-98a9-520e-b1e1-4fe002c1b694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42cb668d-98a9-520e-b1e1-4fe002c1b694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469861} :answer-field/id #uuid "01e0a5d5-4c50-525a-89e6-5d597c736b28" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa0bceb2-f3ad-5f74-bfcd-15e8ad54d9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469862} {:answer/id #uuid "6df557e4-dad7-5074-b3c4-323bb80d5d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa0bceb2-f3ad-5f74-bfcd-15e8ad54d9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469862} :answer-field/id #uuid "e479a106-12d3-59ec-b9b6-52a722604407" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f94b2305-e72d-5eec-b619-8e66f07e8f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469864} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8e0555-1467-55bc-aa6d-82e1f508e311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f94b2305-e72d-5eec-b619-8e66f07e8f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469864} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f23d212-d333-5d3e-861a-acfdd3d94121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d79f788-f655-5287-8607-5b096289e0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-96830" :question/problem "![](images/74/740d578e554cd61bc733079c32c063d41ab4d9dcc775d36f7080ee8e5aa5a622.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $f$ is ${5,10,15}$\n- The codomain of $f$ is ${5,10,12,13,14,15}$\n- The range of $f$ is ${12,13,14}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X={5,10,15},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y={12,13,14},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is ${12,13},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I only.\""}]}
